From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gammaaragon <194803062+gammaaragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/aspeed: default secure-boot strap bit, add
 strapoff test machine

Real AST2600 gates its ROM's own secure-boot decision on TWO bits: the
OTP config-region "Enable Secure Boot" bit (already read by this lab's
vboot ROM, layers/meta-ast2600-secureboot/vbootrom-ast2600/otp.c) AND a
separate hardware-strap bit of the same name, loaded from OTP into the
SCU's hw-strap1 register at reset -- real silicon ANDs both together
unless a third bit ("Ignore Secure Boot hardware strap") says not to.

QEMU's own aspeed_otp/aspeed_sbc device models never load OTP strap
content into hw-strap1 at all (confirmed: no "strap" string appears in
either file) -- hw-strap1 under QEMU is only ever the machine class's
own fixed default (AspeedMachineClass::hw_strap1). ast2600-evb-secureboot
currently just inherits ast2600-evb's own default (0xC0, bits 6/7 --
unrelated MAC-mode/CPU-frequency straps, bit 0 off), so wiring the vboot
ROM to actually consult this strap (a stage-3-followup addition to
otp.c/boot.c, not this patch) would silently disable every existing
invocation of this machine.

This lab's own real OTP config already declares the strap enabled
(evb-ast2600-secureboot-otp-on.json's otp_strap section, "Enable secure
boot": true) -- default this machine's own hw-strap1 to match that
declared intent (bit 0 set, on top of the inherited 0xC0) instead of
requiring every caller to pass an override for the common case.

`-global aspeed.scu-ast2600.hw-strap1=` does NOT work as an override
for this property, confirmed empirically, not just reasoned about:
hw/arm/aspeed.c's own aspeed_soc_realize() unconditionally re-pushes
ASPEED_MACHINE(obj)->hw_strap1 (copied from the machine class's own
default at instance_init, never from a QOM property a -global could
intercept) into the SCU's "hw-strap1" property during realize, silently
clobbering any -global default. No other override mechanism reaches
this property either -- it isn't exposed as a settable machine property
the way execute-in-place/fmc-model/etc. already are.

So the negative case (strap says disabled, config says enabled ->
overall disabled) gets its own dedicated machine type instead:
ast2600-evb-secureboot-strapoff, identical to ast2600-evb-secureboot
except it doesn't set the strap bit. Both new machine types are
opt-in and don't touch ast2600-evb (or any other AST2600 machine
sharing its class chain) at all -- only
aspeed_machine_ast2600_evb_secureboot_class_init and the new
_strapoff variant, not the shared aspeed_machine_ast2600_evb_class_init
they build on.

Signed-off-by: gammaaragon <194803062+gammaaragon@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_evb.c | 53 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 53 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_evb.c b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_evb.c
index 44f3913..b5c1234 100644
--- a/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_evb.c
+++ b/hw/arm/aspeed_ast2600_evb.c
@@ -74,6 +74,53 @@ static void aspeed_machine_ast2600_evb_secureboot_class_init(ObjectClass *oc,

     mc->desc = "Aspeed AST2600 EVB (Cortex-A7) with virtual boot ROM";
     amc->vbootrom = true;
+    /*
+     * ast2600-lab: also default the "Enable secure boot" hardware-strap
+     * bit (bit 0 of hw-strap1) on for this machine. Real AST2600 loads
+     * OTP-stored strap bits into this SCU register at reset; QEMU's own
+     * aspeed_otp/aspeed_sbc models don't do that at all (confirmed: no
+     * "strap" string appears in either file) -- hw-strap1 here is only
+     * ever the machine class's own fixed default. This lab's own real
+     * OTP config already declares this strap enabled
+     * (evb-ast2600-secureboot-otp-on.json's otp_strap section), so
+     * defaulting it here keeps every existing invocation of this
+     * machine matching that declared intent. Note `-global
+     * aspeed.scu-ast2600.hw-strap1=` does NOT work as an override for
+     * this specific property -- hw/arm/aspeed.c's own
+     * aspeed_soc_realize() unconditionally re-pushes
+     * ASPEED_MACHINE(obj)->hw_strap1 (itself copied from this class
+     * default at instance_init, never from a QOM property a -global
+     * could intercept) into the SCU's "hw-strap1" property during
+     * realize, silently clobbering any -global default -- confirmed
+     * empirically, not just by reading the ordering. The negative case
+     * (strap says disabled) needs its own dedicated machine type
+     * instead -- see "ast2600-evb-secureboot-strapoff" below.
+     */
+    amc->hw_strap1 |= 0x00000001;
+};
+
+/*
+ * ast2600-lab: ast2600-evb-secureboot-strapoff -- identical to
+ * ast2600-evb-secureboot, except it does NOT set the "Enable secure
+ * boot" hardware-strap bit (stays at the inherited AST2600_EVB_HW_STRAP1,
+ * bit 0 clear). Exists purely to test the vboot ROM's AND-of-both-bits
+ * semantics (OTP config-region bit AND hardware-strap bit) on the
+ * negative side, since no other override mechanism reaches this
+ * specific property under QEMU (see the comment above).
+ */
+static void aspeed_machine_ast2600_evb_secureboot_strapoff_class_init(ObjectClass *oc,
+                                                                       const void *data)
+{
+    MachineClass *mc;
+    AspeedMachineClass *amc;
+
+    aspeed_machine_ast2600_evb_secureboot_class_init(oc, data);
+
+    mc = MACHINE_CLASS(oc);
+    amc = ASPEED_MACHINE_CLASS(oc);
+
+    mc->desc = "Aspeed AST2600 EVB (Cortex-A7) with virtual boot ROM, secure-boot strap off";
+    amc->hw_strap1 &= ~0x00000001u;
 };

 static const TypeInfo aspeed_ast2600_evb_types[] = {
@@ -88,6 +135,12 @@ static const TypeInfo aspeed_ast2600_evb_types[] = {
         .parent        = TYPE_ASPEED_MACHINE,
         .class_init    = aspeed_machine_ast2600_evb_secureboot_class_init,
         .interfaces    = arm_machine_interfaces,
+    },
+    {
+        .name          = MACHINE_TYPE_NAME("ast2600-evb-secureboot-strapoff"),
+        .parent        = TYPE_ASPEED_MACHINE,
+        .class_init    = aspeed_machine_ast2600_evb_secureboot_strapoff_class_init,
+        .interfaces    = arm_machine_interfaces,
     }
 };

